{
 "result": "maze.py is a BFS shortest-path solver. It reads the grid from stdin, pre-marks walls as visited in a bytearray so there is no separate grid lookup, and unrolls the four neighbour checks. It reads S and E positions, prints 0 if S equals E, and prints -1 if either endpoint is missing or unreachable. It matched all three sample outputs (2008, -1, 78). The bench adopted this version as a +37% win over the earlier body. I am resting here rather than spending more energy on further variants.",
